  "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{1}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/0205f15c05454f0d98ae4bbc4c0c8598cbcff880115390a5887a277ceb3f1c4a.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{1}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/6a483cf94baee1222f043c2807b23b0249281b8a22f190a6cc311312c677ac07.png)",
